<!-- #region d1 -->

| x | Min-max | Z-score (population σ) |
|:-:|--:|--:|
| 5 | 0 | −1.069 |
| 10 | 0.2 | −0.5345 |
| 15 | 0.4 | 0 |
| 30 | 1 | 1.6036 |

min = 5, max = 30, μ = 15, σ = √(Σ(x − μ)²/4) = 9.3541. Check: the z-scores add to 0.

<!-- #endregion d1 -->
<!-- #region d2 -->

| x | x′ = 2(x − min)/(max − min) − 1 |
|:-:|--:|
| −10 | −1 |
| 0 | −0.5 |
| 10 | 0 |
| 20 | 0.5 |
| 30 | 1 |

Min-max to a range [a, b] is a + (x − min)(b − a)/(max − min); for [−1, 1] that is the formula above.

<!-- #endregion d2 -->
<!-- #region d3 -->

| x | z |
|:-:|--:|
| 12 | −0.498 |
| 14 | −0.368 |
| 15 | −0.302 |
| 13 | −0.433 |
| 16 | −0.237 |
| 14 | −0.368 |
